{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/570091-lgbtq-in-cofd-games","id":570091,"title":"LGBTQ+ in CofD games","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-27T03:09:32-07:00","id":570091,"title":"LGBTQ+ in CofD games","content":"We have written 3 games corebooks for 2ED CoD ( or 4, depends on how we look on <b>Beast</b> ). Very nice for the<i> Onyx Path</i> is that they push inclusion in their games in small, nice references in games about non-heteronormative characters. This topic is about collecting them all, for the LGBT+ players and STs glory - because it's <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gay_pride#LGBT_Pride_Month\" target=\"_blank\">Pride Month</a>! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So I will start with two mine favorites:<ul><li><b>Beast: The Primoridal </b>- Character Concepts - p. 87 - <i>\u201cIT manager by day, drag king by night\u201d</i> - It hits me very hard, in positive sense, as myself bisex bear IT Technician. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Also, this lady will have hands full on - work on day, drag by night and Horror in the dreams?!</li> <li><b>Werewolf: The Forsaken 2ED </b>- Touchtones, example - p. 87 - <i>&quot;Example: Picture the dedicated police officer married to his job. He wants to propose to his boyfriend, but it\u2019s just not fair. He\u2019s never home. He\u2019s always in danger. And it\u2019s not like he can just give up the job; it\u2019s who he is. The boyfriend is close enough to touch, but too far to hold. </i>&quot; - It's just so good love story idea, highlighting the topics of Werewolf. With a very nice, gay spin. I love it! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-10-2018, 02:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T06:30:58-07:00","id":570213,"title":"","content":"Two words: Lucy Sulphate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T06:37:20-07:00","id":570218,"title":"","content":"Personally, I've found the Rick &amp; Alessandro's fiction as intriguing, and I've also liked the Requiem's 2nd edition's Touchstone references.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T07:55:36-07:00","id":570258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/570091-lgbtq-in-cofd-games#post570091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>\u201cIT manager by day, drag king by night\u201d</i>[/LIST]</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yes, I loved that. Rocked so damn hard. I remember a drag show that I went to, and there was only one King there. He went up, all cocky and smirking (with an awesome goatee and sideburns, I must add), adjusting his bulge on the way. He performed a Lil' John song, and at the end he raised his arms and swept them out, making it rain fake $100 bills on the first couple rows, like it was a magic trick. Like, no one saw that coming, it was spectacular. Needless to say, he won.<br /> <br /> <br /> So now, I want to post the details of my favorite PC, from my favorite game, Hunter:the Vigil.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td align=\"right\" class=\"text_table_td\"> Concept:</td> <td align=\"left\" class=\"text_table_td\"> Ex SWAT Officer/Drag Queen Diva</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td align=\"right\" class=\"text_table_td\"> Description:</td> <td align=\"left\" class=\"text_table_td\"> Standing tall at 6'8&quot; and holding herself with the posture not just of a trained runway model, but of a natural athlete, Anita Shot is a drag queen with a resume as strong as her baritone singing voice. Possessing angular, masculine features and a hardened, lean figure devoid of fat, and accentuating her strengths with dozens of wigs and loud outfits, and not a single one of them has sleeves. On her left arm is a proudly displayed tattoo of a SWAT badge. On her right arm is an older Army Rangers tattoo.<br /> <br /> She is also an avid gun collector, and her Youtube channel &quot;Anita Shot's Big Girls' Survival Guide&quot; has a large collection of videos teaching proper gun care, handling, and cleaning on a variety of different weapons. She just got sponsored, and her merchandise has finally begun to sell. The money goes back into the community. And since the accident that retired her, she has become aware of deeply rooted, frightening problems that lurk in the community she has served in the past as a police officer, and has come to the conclusion that this community needs her more than she ever knew.<br /> <br /> Away from the internet and out of the clubs, Anita Shot's alter ego, former police officer William Fletch enjoys his free time while not-so-secretly pining for his days before retirement. Still tight with local law enforcement, he is thought of as a hero cop. Anita was around long before he ever left(though not nearly as popular as she is now), and no one bats an eye at his eccentric, glittery persona.</td> </tr> </table></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><br /> I draw things! Wanna check it out? Click on the link below!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy</a><br /> <br /> <i><b>YES! I do commissions! </b></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/848-jtroy","name":"JTroy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar848_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T12:22:00-07:00","id":570422,"title":"","content":"Beast actually has quite a few LGBTQ references in it... which may be part of the reason why it got the &quot;SJW Front!&quot; backlash from some morons... anyway. Taking from the 99% review doc, but I don't recall seeing any of these edited out in the revamp drafts on the Patreon page:<br /> <br /> * Page 50: Sample Nemesis Jess is a genderqueer Eshmaki Nemesis.<br /> <br /> * Page 51: Patrick &amp; Ahmed are a homosexual male couple of Namtaru Beasts (one Collector, one Punisher).<br /> <br /> * Page 134: The example of a High Satiety Hoarder feeding mentions a male homosexual Beast trying to find a very specific sort of man to be his lover.<br /> <br /> <br /> Some Mummy examples I've noticed:<br /> * Book of the Deceived, Page 123: Najaulla-Sen The Merciful One is a female Deceived mentioned as having spent her last incarnation as a male, during which time she suffered from gender dysphoria.<br /> <br /> * Book of the Deceived, Page 124: The Deceived Kefershaitain Stained Hands is genderqueer due to indifference.<br /> <br /> * Cursed Necropolis D.C, Page 56: Hebeny The Bull of Bennu is a FtM transsexual who struggles with the fact that low Memory allows his sahu to show his true gender, whilst higher Memory forces him back to his birth gender.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T12:35:02-07:00","id":570432,"title":"","content":"Promethean 2e is shaping up to be the most queer-friendly game in the entire nWoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T12:43:50-07:00","id":570457,"title":"","content":"I slipped a couple into the Geist RMC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T13:13:27-07:00","id":570483,"title":"","content":"Loli from Geist core and King Queen Jackie Snow from the Fear Makers promise, and the various stuff about Rebuses in Promethian are the only canonical examples I remember off the top of my head but I'm sure there's more.<br /> <br /> In Princess the Queen of Swords is canonically bisexual. There's also a Condition for body dysmorphia that I wrote to support trans characters; while I thought up the Embarrassing Phylactery condition for characters in the metaphorical closet (both ended up in a more general form). There'd be more if the number of Princess characters in the book ever climbed above zero.<br /> <br /> The Staff of Janus believe that being trans is one path to hidden wisdom most people cannot reach - so they have a lot of trans members. Dream Catchers also mentions that Goblin Markets are an alternative to sexual reassignment surgery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T14:00:21-07:00","id":570565,"title":"","content":"Also, Hunter's Dark Era in Japan is going to present a compact of male escorts, which I think are tied to the Kagema of the time (there aren't much details about them, so I can't say for sure)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T15:36:27-07:00","id":570649,"title":"","content":"And of course, the Luna's embrace gift.<br /> <br /> I actually have a concept for a wealthy lesbian ivory claw noble (lodge of kings) couple (who obviously call the gift something else) who used that gift to have children that were both of their's (they took turns being the impregnator and pregnant one).<br /> <br /> I actually really want to explore how the claws handle LGBTQA (don't forget us asexuals, my allo friends) issues, since I imagine that the generation gap on marriage and family issues is tearing that tribe apart.<br /> <br /> Speaking of asexuals and ivory claws, I can't help but remember my character concept from our Wod High school discussion, If only we had managed to get an ST.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T23:22:55-07:00","id":571035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/570091-lgbtq-in-cofd-games?p=570649#post570649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And of course, the Luna's embrace gift.<br /> <br /> I actually have a concept for a wealthy lesbian ivory claw noble (lodge of kings) couple (who obviously call the gift something else) who used that gift to have children that were both of their's (they took turns being the impregnator and pregnant one).</div> </div> </div> </div>Was planing to explore it more in mine games also, on Forsaken side - but how the Pure would call Luna's Embrace with their hate to Moon Goddess? Wolf's Drag? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/570091-lgbtq-in-cofd-games?p=570649#post570649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually really want to explore how the claws handle LGBTQA (don't forget us asexuals, my allo friends) issues, since I imagine that the generation gap on marriage and family issues is tearing that tribe apart.</div> </div> </div> </div>I use Q as Queer in general - I could write all the alphabet of verious orientation or psychosexual identietis each times I mentione community as general, I just use five of them as short. In Poland our associations fighting for equal rights are using now <span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">LGBTQIA and I thing it is a bit tring to hard.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> So anyone's identity not mention by me in discussion - <b>I'm not limited, I know there are very much more variants of human sexuality and I support you all in your decent living and equality in eyes of law . I just will stick to five letters for abrive to ALL non-heteronormatives, for discussion simplisity. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></b><br /> <br /> As to Ivory Claws - would the explore the Luna's Embrace before last 50 decades where LGBTQ come in to global awareness? I think that Hindu Claws could explor this kind of things in the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hijra_(South_Asia)\" target=\"_blank\">Hijra caste</a>.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T01:04:02-07:00","id":571075,"title":"","content":"In <i>Blood and Smoke </i>(page 88), the &quot;Friends with Benefits&quot; example touchstone mentions &quot;you&quot; and a male friend sucking each other off, which to me implies two sets of male genitalia. Feel free to correct me if you know how to suck off a bio girl. :P<br /> <br /> On the following page, the term &quot;her wife&quot; is used to refer to the &quot;Victim's Lover&quot; example touchstone.<br /> <br /> There's also &quot;Mrs. Robinson&quot; from the Mission (page 259), who frequented the 1970's gay club scene as &quot;Angelo Pascual.&quot; The entry on her is vague enough for you to draw your own conclusions, but if she's the creator of the &quot;Mixtape&quot; from the Daeva book, she had at least one romantic relationship with a mortal woman whom she embraced. I like to imagine that she looks like <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qeMFqkcPYcg\" target=\"_blank\">Annie Lennox</a>, but maybe dresses like Bowie's <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0_FAirBN5z8\" target=\"_blank\">Thin White Duke</a>. :P<br /> <br /> EDIT: Upon a quick review of the Mixtape, I don't think it's made explicit what gender &quot;Em&quot; identifies as. They are primarily sexually interested in men (&quot;skinny, long-hair types&quot;), and the creator of the tape suggests that they try to seduce married men, which to me implies that &quot;Em&quot; is most likely a woman, but that isn't necessarily the case. Also, I just noticed that the Mixtape mentions the web, so it's obviously not as old as I thought it might be, and may well not be one of Mrs. Robinson's.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 06-28-2015, 04:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T02:30:17-07:00","id":571090,"title":"","content":"On a related note, as lots of my current GM writing has been taken up with the creation of villains and adversaries for my Mage 2nd Ed campaign, I've been considering the ways in which homophobia and other such related human ills have their place in the game. Some of this relates to issues like how to portray homophobic NPCs and whether homophodic PCs should ever be allowed, etc.<br /> <br /> Other issues I've been considering relate to how the homophobia has a place within the Fallen World. Obviously, Mage is a world of supernal symbols and their mysterious interactions within it, so homophobia is obviously going to be a potent supernal symbol along with tyranny, oppression, etc. <br /> <br /> Hence the question is: does homophobia have a place within the Exarch's plan for humanity. I like the idea that homophobia, transphobia, and hatred for the different and deviant are ways in which the Exarchs divide and rule humanity; one of the myriad ways in which they keep humans at each other throats, reduced to a state of constant strife. There may even possibly be an Exarch/Seal devoted to the symbol itself, perhaps something like 'The Purity' - a symbol of unrelenting Natural Order and the Purity,Stagnation of Natural Law, Its Total and Unchanging Dominion Over All Life - the Eradication of the Deviant and the Unclean. Obviously this symbol has echoes in Eugenics and racial purity, and nasty connections with Nazism and the like. (As you can see, I like my Exarch and the Seers by extension as villains pure and simple, at least conceptually). This raises the opposite idea that the LGBTQ movement and its symbols are also powerful supernal symbols set up by the Oracles!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>Have you seen him? </i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1000-mistere","name":"MisterE","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1000_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T02:57:40-07:00","id":571105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MisterE</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/570091-lgbtq-in-cofd-games?p=571090#post571090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other issues I've been considering relate to how the homophobia has a place within the Fallen World. Obviously, Mage is a world of supernal symbols and their mysterious interactions within it, so homophobia is obviously going to be a potent supernal symbol along with tyranny, oppression, etc.<br /> <br /> Hence the question is: does homophobia have a place within the Exarch's plan for humanity. I like the idea that homophobia, transphobia, and hatred for the different and deviant are ways in which the Exarchs divide and rule humanity; one of the myriad ways in which they keep humans at each other throats, reduced to a state of constant strife. There may even possibly be an Exarch/Seal devoted to the symbol itself, perhaps something like 'The Purity' - a symbol of unrelenting Natural Order and the Purity,Stagnation of Natural Law, Its Total and Unchanging Dominion Over All Life - the Eradication of the Deviant and the Unclean. Obviously this symbol has echoes in Eugenics and racial purity, and nasty connections with Nazism and the like. (As you can see, I like my Exarch and the Seers by extension as villains pure and simple, at least conceptually). This raises the opposite idea that the LGBTQ movement and its symbols are also powerful supernal symbols set up by the Oracles!</div> </div> </div> </div>Is not the general preview of Unity Iron Seal? Her mission is to make everyone the same once mass, without variants. I think that LGBTQ movement is here that same way as racial equality was previously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T03:21:08-07:00","id":571123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MisterE</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/570091-lgbtq-in-cofd-games?p=571090#post571090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a related note, as lots of my current GM writing has been taken up with the creation of villains and adversaries for my Mage 2nd Ed campaign, I've been considering the ways in which homophobia and other such related human ills have their place in the game. Some of this relates to issues like how to portray homophobic NPCs and whether homophodic PCs should ever be allowed, etc.<br /> <br /> Other issues I've been considering relate to how the homophobia has a place within the Fallen World. Obviously, Mage is a world of supernal symbols and their mysterious interactions within it, so homophobia is obviously going to be a potent supernal symbol along with tyranny, oppression, etc.<br /> <br /> Hence the question is: does homophobia have a place within the Exarch's plan for humanity. I like the idea that homophobia, transphobia, and hatred for the different and deviant are ways in which the Exarchs divide and rule humanity; one of the myriad ways in which they keep humans at each other throats, reduced to a state of constant strife. There may even possibly be an Exarch/Seal devoted to the symbol itself, perhaps something like 'The Purity' - a symbol of unrelenting Natural Order and the Purity,Stagnation of Natural Law, Its Total and Unchanging Dominion Over All Life - the Eradication of the Deviant and the Unclean. Obviously this symbol has echoes in Eugenics and racial purity, and nasty connections with Nazism and the like. (As you can see, I like my Exarch and the Seers by extension as villains pure and simple, at least conceptually). This raises the opposite idea that the LGBTQ movement and its symbols are also powerful supernal symbols set up by the Oracles!</div> </div> </div> </div>Diving humanity by making them hate each other and fear other groups who are different from them? The sounds like something the General would do. Sure, big wars is where you can see Her hand the most easily, but every big war starts from a small strife- that the other person is different, and posses a threat to your righteous way of life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T03:43:32-07:00","id":571143,"title":"","content":"I still think xenophobia, on basis, is the Unity kind of thing:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Seers of Throne</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The Unity</b><br /> <i>The All Encompassing, the King of Obedience, the Indivisible</i><br /> <br /> The Unity cleanses humanity of individuality. People are weak alone, but together, acting under one will, they might taste the divinity they lost when they Fell. They need only sacrifice freedom. He whispers of the joys of conformity and manifests through impersonal institutions such as banks and governments. Humans are cells of the leviathan. Her number is one. His Prelacy is Obligation. He is the patron of the Hegemonic Ministry and is said to rule over Seers\u2019 use of the Mind Arcanum.</div> </div> </div> </div>Making &quot;Others&quot; in the society is exactly what Unity would do. Also, she shackles the Freedom - like the Freedom to love who you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T04:36:39-07:00","id":571163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/570091-lgbtq-in-cofd-games?p=571143#post571143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still think xenophobia, on basis, is the Unity kind of thing:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Making &quot;Others&quot; in the society is exactly what Unity would do. Also, she shackles the Freedom - like the Freedom to love who you want.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I see your point, wyrdhamster, there is definitely some crossover there between the Unity and my conception of the purity. But I think the difference lies in the Purity's insistence upon the nasty idea of purity and cleanliness as moral forces. I see the the Unity as potential embracing diversity quite easily, as the example of the diverse body of an organism, where all the very different organs and tissues are united in under a common authority. I could imagine an 'ideal' world for the Unity, a bureaucratic authoritarian nightmare police state that perfectly tolerates people of any sexual identity so long as they're part of the common unity and know their place. I think societies have attempted to define a 'correct' social order where people who we would categorize as LGBTQ have their proper place. <br /> <br /> The difference in the Purity and where the Purity's central emphasis lies, is not upon rebelling against an authority and its commands, but rather with that all consuming hatred and fear of the different and diverse that seems to sicken those fear the 'other', where that other might be foreigners, migrants, the mentally deficient, different or 'impure' races, or people who are just unclean and 'unnatural'. It about deviancy as a crime against a pure and pristine natural order, deviancy as a moral crime and a corruption - a pollution. Its the sort of moral pollution that fires the anger of neo-Nazi white supremacists and Eugenicists, as well as the anger of every of homophobe. <br /> <br /> So the central themes/oppositions would be: pure/impure, clean/unclean, healthy/deviant, pristine/corrupt. The Purity attempt to demonise and exclude and persecute the deviant and the unclean, so as to maintain the purity of whatever group is doing the exclusion. The Nazis and their template of racial purity are the archetypal basis for the Purity. It doesn't matter one jot whether Jews, homosexuals, gypsies or the mental deficient might follow or bow before the unifying authority of the Nazi state and obey its laws. The ideology of the state has already marked them out as ESSENTIALLY WRONG and a pollution of the moral natural order of the German people. Thus they only 'moral' solution for such an ideology is to &quot;purge the unclean&quot; and maintain purity. That's all that matters is Purity. Another example might be Victorian asylums and their treatments 'moral illnesses' like homosexuality being rated alongside their treatment of physical ailments. Aspects of this can also be seen in other exclusionary social orders, such as Old Testament purity laws (which also controls female purity), the Varna caste system of Vedic Law and its exclusion of the 'untouchables', eugenic views of human nature, etc. <br /> <br /> But hey, that's just my feeling; you may prefer to lump this together under either the Unity or the General.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>Have you seen him? </i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1000-mistere","name":"MisterE","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1000_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T05:49:22-07:00","id":571230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/570091-lgbtq-in-cofd-games?p=571143#post571143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still think xenophobia, on basis, is the Unity kind of thing:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Making &quot;Others&quot; in the society is exactly what Unity would do. Also, she shackles the Freedom - like the Freedom to love who you want.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, the way I understood the Unity is that he is seeking to eliminate the &quot;others&quot; be assimilation. He is the one to promise you you don't have to be different- that being different is wrong. We are all humans, and so we are all the same. Trying to be different harms that special harmony that mankind has- you should just stop be yourself and be like the rest. He is the one who wants you to stay in the closet, the one who hates Pride Parades because it shows that not all people are the same- it is the other side of homophobia. If the General is about others hating you for being different from them, the Unity is about you hating yourself for being different. He also represent the more &quot;moderate homophob&quot;- those who say that it is ok for gay people to exist, but why are they so loud? Why can't they just act like the rest? There must be some problem with them if they can't just accept that at least acting like everyone else is better.<br /> <br /> This is the main difference between the General and the Unity- the first would admit to hate you, and she would never let you live in peace. The second would act as if he loves you, and would even offer you a way out- you just need to leave everything which makes you &quot;you&quot; behind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T05:49:27-07:00","id":571231,"title":"","content":"<b>Promethean 2nd Ed</b> has a few references to non-straight/non-cis characters, but of course that game isn't out yet. <br /> <br /> Opening fiction for<b> Mythologies</b>, the POV character is a gay man. <br /> <br /> Likewise, opening fiction for <b>Legacies: The Ancient</b>, the POV character is...probably pansexual, although he thinks of himself as straight in the beginning of the story and discovers otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T05:51:13-07:00","id":571232,"title":"","content":"and there's also one of the example Acanthus in 2nd edition's Preview about a straight man who starts his Awakening by sleeping for another man for the first time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T07:50:37-07:00","id":571304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/570091-lgbtq-in-cofd-games?p=571035#post571035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Was planing to explore it more in mine games also, on Forsaken side - but how the Pure would call Luna's Embrace with their hate to Moon Goddess? Wolf's Drag? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I use Q as Queer in general - I could write all the alphabet of verious orientation or psychosexual identietis each times I mentione community as general, I just use five of them as short. In Poland our associations fighting for equal rights are using now <span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">LGBTQIA and I thing it is a bit tring to hard.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> So anyone's identity not mention by me in discussion - <b>I'm not limited, I know there are very much more variants of human sexuality and I support you all in your decent living and equality in eyes of law . I just will stick to five letters for abrive to ALL non-heteronormatives, for discussion simplisity. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></b><br /> <br /> As to Ivory Claws - would the explore the Luna's Embrace before last 50 decades where LGBTQ come in to global awareness? I think that Hindu Claws could explor this kind of things in the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hijra_(South_Asia)\" target=\"_blank\">Hijra caste</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I Understand, I imagine any acronym that included ALL non-heteronormitives would be way too long and clunky.<br /> <br /> Given that animistic/shamanistic religions generally seem to be more okay with non-cisgender folk, I would imagine that maybe the claws were okay with trans folk as long as they still reproduced with an opposite sex partner (using whatever the pure call luna's embrace to change their sex to match their gender first, of course). but same sex couples weren't approved of by the tribe until more recently.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T12:02:16-07:00","id":571725,"title":"","content":"Oh man, I could see the agents of the Unity running one of those &quot;gay conversion therapy&quot; camps (or whatever the preferred nomenclature is). With the aid of magic, the therapy could be frighteningly effective (though it would probably require regular treatments to overcome dissonance), while leaving the subject riddled with dysphoria.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T23:38:13-07:00","id":572362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/570091-lgbtq-in-cofd-games?p=571075#post571075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also &quot;Mrs. Robinson&quot; from the Mission (page 259), who frequented the 1970's gay club scene as &quot;Angelo Pascual.&quot; The entry on her is vague enough for you to draw your own conclusions, but if she's the creator of the &quot;Mixtape&quot; from the Daeva book, she had at least one romantic relationship with a mortal woman whom she embraced. I like to imagine that she looks like <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qeMFqkcPYcg\" target=\"_blank\">Annie Lennox</a>, but maybe dresses like Bowie's <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0_FAirBN5z8\" target=\"_blank\">Thin White Duke</a>. :P<br /> <br /> EDIT: Upon a quick review of the Mixtape, I don't think it's made explicit what gender &quot;Em&quot; identifies as. They are primarily sexually interested in men (&quot;skinny, long-hair types&quot;), and the creator of the tape suggests that they try to seduce married men, which to me implies that &quot;Em&quot; is most likely a woman, but that isn't necessarily the case. Also, I just noticed that the Mixtape mentions the web, so it's obviously not as old as I thought it might be, and may well not be one of Mrs. Robinson's.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm so glad somebody put together that Mrs. Robinson is the author of &quot;Mixtape!&quot; So, so glad. You'll also note that Mrs. Robinson is the Daeva signature character. Dressed classy for a release party or something in her splat portrait, but I like to imagine her with a more classic punk rock or new-wave-to-the-grave look when she's all casual.<br /> <br /> There's also a trans man elsewhere in the cities chapter, but it seemed like he wouldn't want to talk about it, so the clue is very subtle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 06-29-2015, 02:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T02:45:22-07:00","id":572483,"title":"","content":"Nice! It's cool to have a picture to attach to the name; not what I was imagining, but just as good.<br /> <br /> I really liked the stuff on the Mission from the Daeva book, and I was super excited to see the setting make a return in <i>Blood and Smoke</i>. My personal version of the setting incorporates Xiao Jun Jie from <i>Bloodlines: The Chosen</i> and the story of John Carnon from <i>Circle of the Crone</i> as well. I find that the latter actually fits really well with the historical bits described in the Mission interview in <i>Kiss of the Succubus</i>; Carnon's rampage could very well have been the last straw that led to the Sanctified crackdown circa 1970.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T05:18:51-07:00","id":572530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/570091-lgbtq-in-cofd-games?p=572483#post572483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nice! It's cool to have a picture to attach to the name; not what I was imagining, but just as good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. I honestly considered dressing her more the way I figure she dresses casually. but for the signature character piece, you want at least some level of classic. So I gave her a dress partly inspired by my favorite* <i>Vampire </i>cover: <i>City of the Damned.</i> Is the red silk or blood? Who can say?<br /> <br /> * I think it's my favorite, I don't exactly keep a ranked list.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T10:05:39-07:00","id":572831,"title":"","content":"DtD has a lesbian couple dealing with sexual harassment... to the detriment of the harasser. In addition, there's the general fact for most demons gender is a sometimes thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","user":"Agentwestmer","date":". 05-07-2018, 01:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T10:09:13-07:00","id":572835,"title":"","content":"I'm trying to guess who the other signature characters are supposed to be... I figure the Gangrel has to be Count F*cking Dracula... I'm tempted to think that the Mekhet is the compiler of the Mekhet book (blanking on her name at the moment). No idea on the other two...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T11:14:47-07:00","id":572933,"title":"","content":"talking about DtD- isn't there a fiction in the book which presented a male-covered angel who Fell after falling in love with a man? I must say that one of the things I like the most about the way non-straight characters are presented in nWoD is that they aren't presented as regular people- their concept isn't revolved around their sexual orientation. You couldn't tell the angel's gender in that fiction until he actually Fell and the &quot;it&quot; turned to &quot;he&quot;. I really appreciate that style, because it really shows that even non-straight people not only, but are regular human beings (or vampires. Or werewolves. or soul-stealing-reality-twisting-bio-mechanical-monster-escaped-from-a-mad-god-thingy)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T11:45:09-07:00","id":572980,"title":"","content":"Ah, here's one I almost forgot from <i>Blood and Smoke</i>: Cardinal Inglorious I, the founder of the Mission, took a lover from among the native Californian vampires he encountered in the San Francisco area, &quot;a man called Hummingbird.&quot; Not just gay lovers, <i>18th century</i> <i>interracial gay lovers</i>. I'd compliment the Cardinal on his progressiveness if it weren't for the whole creepy cult vibe surrounding the whole thing.<br /> <br /> And suddenly I'm having visions of a really cheesy porno starring guys in powdered wigs called &quot;18th Century Interracial Gay Lovers&quot;...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T13:56:36-07:00","id":576748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/570091-lgbtq-in-cofd-games?p=572835#post572835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm trying to guess who the other signature characters are supposed to be... I figure the Gangrel has to be Count F*cking Dracula... I'm tempted to think that the Mekhet is the compiler of the Mekhet book (blanking on her name at the moment). No idea on the other two...</div> </div> </div> </div>The 2e signature characters are;<br /> <br /> Daeva: Mrs. Robinson<br /> Gangrel: Count Dracula<br /> Mekhet: Frances Black<br /> Nosferatu: Jenny Shakes<br /> Ventrue: The Mogul","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T14:01:25-07:00","id":576753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/570091-lgbtq-in-cofd-games?p=576748#post576748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The 2e signature characters are;<br /> <br /> Daeva: Mrs. Robinson<br /> Gangrel: Count Dracula<br /> Mekhet: Frances Black<br /> Nosferatu: Jenny Shakes<br /> Ventrue: The Mogul</div> </div> </div> </div>Would it be possible to find out what fictions or books these characters appear in?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T15:01:14-07:00","id":576799,"title":"","content":"As far as I know, Mrs. Robinson has never appeared in fiction, per se, but she is confirmed as the maker of the Mixtape that appears in the Daeva clanbook, which is interesting in its own right as an introduction to kindred society from the perspective of a vampire in the Mission. She's given a short description in Blood and Smoke as well, in the section on the Mission.<br /> <br /> Count Dracula (not <i>the </i>Count, but rather a Gangrel who claims to be his heir) pops up in a few different places, including the Gangrel clanbook and the story <i>Noblesse Oblige</i> in the Strix Chronicle Anthology.<br /> <br /> Frances Black is the in-universe compiler of the documents making up the Mekhet clanbook, and features in many of the fiction pieces therein. She is also mentioned in some of the other clanbooks, but I don't think she makes an appearance.<br /> <br /> I honestly have no idea where Jenny Shakes comes from... it's possible she's a new character who will appear in some future book...<br /> <br /> The Mogul appears as an interviewee in the Ventrue clanbook. He introduces himself as Cyrus, but that seems to be just one of his many aliases (possibly his &quot;business name&quot;).<br /> <br /> <br /> Incidentally, I <i>really</i> want to make an actual prop out of that mixtape, but there's no way I could pull off an appropriate voice. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 07-02-2015, 06:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T15:46:25-07:00","id":576822,"title":"","content":"Count Fucking Dracula has his own PDF, as is only fitting. Tragically but amusingly bowdlerized.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T15:53:24-07:00","id":576841,"title":"","content":"I believe Jenny was confirmed as a new character before Blood and Smoke came out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T16:14:13-07:00","id":576874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/570091-lgbtq-in-cofd-games?p=576822#post576822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Tragically but amusingly bowdlerized.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. I never knew of the word &quot;bowdlerized&quot;. I'm gonna get some mileage out of this one. Thanks for that.<br /> Also, I have the PDF. Hows it been bowdlerized?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T20:45:28-07:00","id":577055,"title":"","content":"Way back in Ancient Mysteries and Ancient Bloodlines you had Nanshe Iltani, and her lover and student, Arahunaa, who was seduced away from her by En Isiratuu when he visited the Temple of Nanaja in Ur. Though it was all very tragic and, at least according to legend, nearly wiped out the Kindred and Iltani is probably mostly remembered for her venomous bloodline.<br /> <br /> Firewalker, James Deuel, the glue that holds the Black Moon eXtreme pack together and keeps them ready to hunt vampires.<br /> <br /> Frank Tate, the signature character of the Lodge of the Crossroads.<br /> <br /> Very little sexuality of any kind in werewolf, unfortunately. Hopefully the new edition will help with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":".  There was more of a shift in focus than the removal of the unihar 07-03-2015, 01:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T05:17:52-07:00","id":577243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/570091-lgbtq-in-cofd-games?p=576799#post576799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I honestly have no idea where Jenny Shakes comes from... it's possible she's a new character who will appear in some future book...</div> </div> </div> </div>Jenny Shakes is from a chapter cut from The Danse Macabre.<br /> You can find it <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/dropped-like-a-stone/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, fo' free.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Italian nuisance. English is my second language, so be patient!<br /> <br /> <b>My homebrew:</b><br /> <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/270766-domain-light-from-a-dead-star-rome\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">[VtR 2e] Light From a Dead Star: Rome</span></a></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1117941-hunting-ground-the-past-is-another-country-rome\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#8B4513\"><b>[WtF 2e] The Past Is Another Country: Rome</b></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3765-snesferatu","name":"SNESferatu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3765_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T20:51:08-07:00","id":588809,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't mind more BDSM characters. I'm of the school of thought that LGBTQA should be LGBTQABDSM. As someone who conciders himself Dominate as a sexual orination, it would be nice to see a Dom character would isn't an asshole. <br /> <br /> I know alot of people including in the BDSM community don't see it as a sexual orination, but my sexuality did not make sense to me until I realized it. When I was younger I had alot of predominately sexual attraction to males, which had me thinking I might be Gay, then I realized I was still attracted to women so I thought I was bi, then my interest in man waned, and I was left wondering who the fuck was going on. I was afraid to talk to anyone because I didn't want to risk being used as a poster man for Gay Conversion Therapy homophobic bullshit.<br /> <br /> Then I had a realization that maybe BDSM could be a sexual orination and looked up the idea the net and saw other people felt the same way. Some people used the term BDSM an Orination, while others Kink, but personally I found BDSM included multiple sexual orinations and Kink was too broad, but after reading that the human brain has circuts for both Domination and Submission, but usually only one is fully wired up, which backs up BDSM sexual orination as a sexual orination I decided calling myself a Dominate felt right and for the first time in my life it felt like my sexual identity made SENSE! Its a good feeling. <br /> <br /> I want BDSM recognized as a group of sexual orinations, not just for my ego, but because in Canada, Sexual Orinations are protected under the Constitution, as a Analogous Grounds, as recognized by the Supreme Court, which would give legal protections to the BDSM community and encourage education about it in the general community. I knew some stuff, but for the most part I had to figure out shit for myself via trial and error and that's not ideal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T21:06:18-07:00","id":588827,"title":"","content":"Jesus fucking Christ. 'Dom' is not an identity, it's a fetish/kink, and experiences no comparable oppression with the marginalized groups covered by LGBTQA. As someone who is both queer and kinky, one is nothing like the other.<br /> <br /> Off-topic as hell, anyway. Your post has nothing to do with the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> An in the name of staying on-topic, I adore how shamelessly queer PtC 2e seems to be shaping up to be. Gender and sexuality fit the narrative of self-discovery and ostracization so well that it seems unnatural not to include it in the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T21:27:46-07:00","id":588846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/570091-lgbtq-in-cofd-games?p=588827#post588827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jesus fucking Christ. 'Dom' is not an identity, it's a fetish/kink, and experiences no comparable oppression with the marginalized groups covered by LGBTQA. As someone who is both queer and kinky, one is nothing like the other.<br /> <br /> Off-topic as hell, anyway. Your post has nothing to do with the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> An in the name of staying on-topic, I adore how shamelessly queer PtC 2e seems to be shaping up to be. Gender and sexuality fit the narrative of self-discovery and ostracization so well that it seems unnatural not to include it in the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I always felt that it was always better applied as an allegory for autism and learning disabilities (probably projecting, I'll admit), I can certainly see the parallels in your interpretation as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T21:47:50-07:00","id":588865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/570091-lgbtq-in-cofd-games?p=576874#post576874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh. I never knew of the word &quot;bowdlerized&quot;. I'm gonna get some mileage out of this one. Thanks for that.<br /> Also, I have the PDF. Hows it been bowdlerized?</div> </div> </div> </div>Either because it was originally published as an insert in a broader magazine that might have different content standards, or just as a hilarious joke to underscore how over the top it is, all the curses in Count Fucking Dracula's mini-supplement are blacked out. What really makes it amusing is that all the curses are still printed normally, and there's just an additional layer overlaid on top of them blacking them out. Since it's a PDF, this means a) the reader loads the censorship layer after it's already displayed the text layer, and b) you get the normal text just by using the text selection tool, not to mention c) the word &quot;Fucking&quot; in the title bar is not completely obscured by the blackout and can still be read just by its edges.<br /> <br /> Explaining it kills the joke, of course.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/570091-lgbtq-in-cofd-games?p=588846#post588846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I always felt that it was always better applied as an allegory for autism and learning disabilities (probably projecting, I'll admit), I can certainly see the parallels in your interpretation as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>A good allegory is often a flexible allegory. In the case of Promethean I think added layers improve the work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T06:09:48-07:00","id":589102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/570091-lgbtq-in-cofd-games?p=577055#post577055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Very little sexuality of any kind in werewolf, unfortunately. Hopefully the new edition will help with that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably because sex between werewolves was a no-no in 1st ed. Anyone's guess as to what we'll see now that it's not verboten anymore. (I was just thinking, I've written a bunch of WtF fiction, why haven't I written more sex, I always do that...oh, right, unihar.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-