"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T00:05:19-07:00","id":593612,"title":"","content":"I think this is in the spirit of this thread, but if not I apologise in advance.<br /> <br /> Given how important a lot of people seem to think LGBQTIA issues are to the World of Darkness, which certainly seems to make sense, I've looked back over my games and I've never really included anything remotely of that nature (oddly enough, I've decided to make my current character bisexual, but that hasn't come up even a little, so it's little better than head-canon. Don't know if that counts or not). So, realising that I've neglected this whole spectrum of human experience in my games, I started thinking about it could be included in a respectful and interesting way that actually contributes to the story... and then ran out after &quot;make some NPCs incidentally non-cis-heterosexual if it comes up&quot;, which I'm guessing is probably fine in itself, but seems a bit limited.<br /> <br /> Can anyone give me any pointers as to how I can use these ideas/experiences/orientations/whatever-they're-called-I'm-bad-at-terminology's to enhance my stories or expand their range?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T01:01:01-07:00","id":593624,"title":"","content":"Well, are you yourself in any way non-normative by societal standards? Being part of a non-majority group can mean belonging to tight-knit community. People who also share some of your experiences or are at least empathic towards those things you have to go through. Sometimes groups like that can be a cross between family, support group, local community, maybe even professional network. <br /> <br /> We're all human networks after all, and while you can reduce it down to &quot;who I'm related to/who I work with/who I am friends with&quot; you might consider how different aspects of your identity inform that.<br /> <br /> Like, say you live in a particular neighborhood, and you're a trans person of color. It's very possible that you're involved in some kind of private community with other trans people of color, or you might have some kind of formal or informal group based upon that. Maybe this group isn't totally visible, because it's online, or done through a medium which prohibits people from gathering easily and becoming associated with one another.<br /> <br /> So you're part of that community, and you get your Awakening, or your Embrace or whatever. That could force you apart from that community, and that community is, in all likelihood, <i>very </i>interested in figuring out what happened to one of their community members.<br /> <br /> I remember when I was in college (I'm a bi male) we had special meetings of the people in the associated colleges that were also bi or LGBT+, and I met a bunch of my close friends through that organization.<br /> <br /> It can be easy to discount how your sexuality or your gender identity might play a part in your social groups when it does so &quot;invisibly&quot; as can be the case when you're cisgendered or heterosexual, but they can be very important to people in a world that seems at times to be very hostile towards the very existence of people who defy heteronormativity.<br /> <br /> ***<br /> <br /> I guess a way to trim that all down is to think about how being LGBT+ might effect a character or an NPC's friends, family or livelihood, incorporating that isn't making it the focus but acknowledging how these things play a part in our lives.<br /> <br /> Casual inclusion can be cool too, though. Having characters who are in some way non-heteronormative in your games where it's mentioned incidentally (The NPC casually mentions her wife, or her girlfriend in conversation, maybe the next link in an investigation into a missing person is the queer community they belonged to, etc.)<br /> <br /> These things are parts of our lives after all. It's another way to create NPCs with those inner lives that can make PCs interested in interacting with them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T01:14:03-07:00","id":593629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/570091-lgbtq-in-cofd-games?p=593612#post593612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can anyone give me any pointers as to how I can use these ideas/experiences/orientations/whatever-they're-called-I'm-bad-at-terminology's to enhance my stories or expand their range?</div> </div> </div> </div>Orientation, most of the time. If you talk about trans people, sexual identity is much more accurate.<br /> <br /> And what you could run idea with? I give an example - year ago I come to the same thoughts as you. I wanted to include gay bear NPC to a game. And as I was running <b>Werewolf</b> then, I made gay WAREbear. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> The game was all-male players in group, so I chosen groups leader character as sexual fascination for NPC - because the player described his character as perfect mucle bear lumberjack type ( well, character was ex-athlete, now lumberjack, so it fit <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ). But the NPC I run normally, most of the time - he was &quot;lost cub&quot; who left his homeland ( where game took place ) after massacre of his family and gone to city to live as typical &quot;club bear&quot;. He even had once a werefox boyfriend that &quot;teached him some tricks&quot;. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> But in the game, he worked as healer ( as bears are known from mythology ) and ally to the group. Just from time to time he stared in to leader character, maybe thrown a one or two flirt jokes about them two. In the end, players were really sorry, as the NPC were killed by their enemies for the ritual sacrifice. Ach, good times...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T14:01:25-07:00","id":595002,"title":"","content":"One question is how common is sex and romance in your game. If it is fairly common, and your game is modern, it is super easy. Have some NPCs be attracted to each other who are same sex. Done. All four of my games have had gay male and female characters come up, and 3/4 have had transpeople. The Majority of PCs in <i>Balance of Shadows, Night Train Detective Agency,</i> and <i>Golden Eagle</i> are somewhere on the spectrum, and <i>Malibu Dream House </i>is 50/50.<br /> <br /> In a game where romance nearly never happens, it is harder. The simplest, least obtrusive way is have NPCs mention a wife/husband that indicates a same sex pairing...a shopkeeper mentions her wife called, and ally needs to have his husband do something for him. Understated, but indicating existence. A friend wants to schedule something around a date with a girl she has and really does not want to mess this up, or a different friend asks if he thinks a mutual acquaintance might be gay as he is shy/afraid to ask, if you want to be slightly more direct.<br /> <br /> Transpersons are often easier, take an NPC, make them trans. Frequently, it is at least somewhat noticeable. But don't make a big deal of it. And don't try to use &quot;subtle cues&quot; either, that often turns out offensive. Just say something like &quot;Beverly meets you inside the building, she is dressed in a red suit with a feminine cut, has long black hair and is trans. She is holding the briefcase and smiles when she recognizes you, but looks behind you to make sure you are not followed.&quot;<br /> <br /> Gay culture can be trickier to include for people without much exposure to it. it is, fortunately, pretty easy to work in LGBTQs without having to touch on it too much. Unless you plan to look into it a great deal, I'd skip that part. Honestly I know young homosexual men and women who have no exposure really whatsoever to it with the greater acceptance of LGBTQs going on.<br /> <br /> My caution would be to avoid stereotypes, especially negative ones. Predatory gays and lesbians is a big one, don't go with that. Don't make gay men effeminate jokes. Hard Gays and Bull Dykes are out there, but not every gay man or lesbian is one or the other. Transpeople trying to &quot;trick&quot; people is downright offensive. Try not to make every LGBTQ a criminal or sex worker. There are LGBTQ criminals and sex workers, sure, and including some is fine. But don't make them the majority, the majority of visible ones, or the first ones the PCs meet. Avoid the slutty/indecisive bi stereotype. Most bisexual and pansexual persons know what they like, thank you, and their libido is not necessarily better or worse than any other. Have some idea of the difference between transvestites, drag queens, and transgender persons. If you are unsure, just include transpersons who are a gender other than what is on their birth certificate and want to be treated as the gender they present themselves as, and leave out drag shows.<br /> <br /> If NPCs can be LGBTQs without their whole personality being &quot;gay&quot; or &quot;trans&quot; or something, you are on the right track. They can be activists, but not every LGBTQ is.<br /> <br /> Hope the above helps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T19:22:20-07:00","id":595237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron Samedi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/570091-lgbtq-in-cofd-games?p=595002#post595002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Transpersons are often easier, take an NPC, make them trans. Frequently, it is at least somewhat noticeable. But don't make a big deal of it. And don't try to use &quot;subtle cues&quot; either, that often turns out offensive. Just say something like &quot;Beverly meets you inside the building, she is dressed in a red suit with a feminine cut, has long black hair and is trans. She is holding the briefcase and smiles when she recognizes you, but looks behind you to make sure you are not followed.&quot;<br /> <br /> Gay culture can be trickier to include for people without much exposure to it. it is, fortunately, pretty easy to work in LGBTQs without having to touch on it too much. Unless you plan to look into it a great deal, I'd skip that part. Honestly I know young homosexual men and women who have no exposure really whatsoever to it with the greater acceptance of LGBTQs going on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the advice (that includes wyrdhamster and Leet!), it's been pretty helpful.<br /> <br /> Interestingly, it was the trans I was mostly baffled about. I used to work in a gay bar, which wasn't a fair representation of gay people <i>at all</i> (at least, according to the people who worked there who were gay), but somehow it did give me some exposure, so I can generalise to a somewhat more 'standard model', if you get my meaning (reading over that it sounds really offensive. Not my intent!). But trans, I have very little interaction with; there were only a couple at the bar - and I think they were more the cross-dressing-for-sexual-thrill type than 'proper' trans - and the only other trans person I've interacted with was a colossal tool; calling me a Nazi (literally) every time I disagreed with their <i>quite</i> far-left-wing politics, no matter how polite I tried to be, or even if I wasn't actually addressing them at the time. So I don't even have a base to work from, even a flawed one: I don't <i>get</i> trans the way I get being homo- or bisexual or other varients of that type. I have no psychological model to work from. What do trans people go through? Is it that they feel like the opposite gender, or that they adopt the social mores of that gender despite being comfortable with their biological sex? I know it's supposed to be a spectrum and there's lots of variability, just as there is with any human category, but that doesn't help create decent characters since I don't know what that spectrum <i>is </i>or what the variables are. Apparently wearing the clothes of the opposite gender isn't always a trans thing, so I can't even use that... deeply confused.<br /> <br /> <u>OK, I can't re-write the above so it's not offensive. I promise I've done my best, but the fact is I just don't have the language or knowledge to do it properly and still ask the questions I want to ask. I assure everyone reading that my intent is not to cause offense, and if I have, it's due to my own ignorance, and I apologise profusely.</u>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T20:04:16-07:00","id":595253,"title":"","content":"Thing is, the less of a &quot;model&quot; you have, the best. Not just because there are a variation, but because this variation can run almost any experience you can imagine. Just mix freely how the character feel about each aspect of his identity, his body, his life.<br /> <br /> In my games I already did a lot of variations, both as ST and as player. Most of my favourite characters aren't cis. The secret is that there are no secret, just people.<br /> <br /> You can try starting to think of your character just as a standard char. Think about his sexuality first in the most common experiences: is he a virgin? Does he have heavy expectations? Problems in a previous relationship? Is he very sexualy active or think about sex just once in a whyle? Go ahead with questions that you could ask to anyone, those are the really important questions.<br /> <br /> When you're done, just add &quot;quirks&quot; you find interesting to this char and think of how they could interact with the other answers. In its core, he's a human being, like anyone else, even about his sexuality. Or gender identity, by the way. They're not the same thing.<br /> <br /> So don't ask. Just think, and if you have an idea, give it a try thinking about this char as a normal person at the core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T00:15:45-07:00","id":595451,"title":"","content":"Simply put, Trans people are people whose correct gender is not the gender they are born with, it is the gender they present themselves as. They just want to be treated as the appropriate gender and want to live their lives as that gender. That's pretty much transpeople in a nutshell, and they, <i>we</i>, are all too often treated very poorly. <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hmoAX9f6MOc\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a> is a video from &quot;Last Week Tonight&quot; which discusses a great deal about transpersons and what we face in the world despite moving ahead. If you are normally averse to LWT, I can say this segment only deals with transpeople specifically, not politics outside the subject.<br /> <br /> Some people (including all transpeople) are genderqueer, which is to say they have a gender outside cisgender norms, but are not necessarily as straightforward as being a transperson. Some feel, for example, they are a third gender. Some are agendered. Some are genderfluid. It is difficult for me without as much personal experience to speak intelligently about them. I prefer to allow them to speak for themselves when possible.<br /> <br /> Drag Queens are a thing in gay culture (though not all are gay) who tend to be somewhat outrageous and theatrical. Drag Queens (usually) identify as male, their persona being a female and often outrageous for humorous or amusing purpose. There is not (usually) a real sexual component to them, though for some there are. There are a lot of caveats there, but I have known several Drag Queens (more than transpeople IRL, honestly) and not all were gay, and some had a sexual component to them (one was only interested in men in his persona, for example) but most were gay men with a persona they enjoyed being outrageous with.<br /> <br /> Tranvestites enjoy wearing clothes of the opposite sex, often for gratification but not necessarily. Some are Drag Queens, most are not. Some are just more comfortable in women's clothes but do not feel that they are the wrong sex. Like with some of the other parts of the Genderqueer spectrum, I feel less qualified to discuss them.<br /> <br /> If I misrepresented anyone in the above post I am sorry. Please correct me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T02:08:09-07:00","id":595488,"title":"","content":"In the end, any label put limits in something that is limitless, that's why I prefer by myself to avoid them. If you can think of a human experience in that regard, you can be sure someone out there is LIVING it. Like, you could have a &quot;male born&quot; character that only in his mid-twenties start to realise he never felt like a &quot;he&quot;, and is almost thirty when can be sure, finaly, that she feels like a woman inside. But she's not sure if she wants to get rid of her genitals or something like that, she doesn't quite feel like a woman traped in a man's body, but instead that something is right with each gender, even if she's at least sure she's a woman. Oh, and she likes women, mind you. Add spice by making this char already married with a straight woman she loves, but doesn't have the slightest idea of how this wife of her will react if told that her husband actualy feels like a woman and wants to be one.<br /> <br /> Just let your mind play with ideas and with the limits of human experience. Then get the result and imagine a real, normal, full and complex person that just have this in place of expected identity or sexuality, but is otherwise whatever a common person could be. A genderqueer can be anything, even homophobic. You can even give to your character the SAME doubts about the issue you have yourself. Some do have those doubts and a thousand more. Some do not.<br /> <br /> You can them just use hose characters as normal people and watch your players react. It seems poor at first as an inclusive game, but believe, just to make those people apear as normal, with nothing to expect from them just for this, you'll both treat the question with respect and make your players and yourself think about it. And maybe your players will surprise you, be with receptiveness or prejudice, maybe not from them, but from the characters, and them all you have to think is how this perfectly normal person would react. And if you don't know how to react, just play the part and let the character not knowing, either.<br /> <br /> A next stage could be making relationships relevant in your game, an exercise you can and should start with common heterosexual couples. It can range from a passionate crime to simply have a character that need to account for his relationship when scheduling his week. An NPC can call the PCs to negotiate something in his house, where his familly can be used as background, and some of them can come to the fore and become relevant NPCs themselfs. Them you start to blend in some queergender content, and work from there.<br /> <br /> The closing of the circle comes when you add the reactions of the world at large. And that doesn't have to be allways the same way, either. Some people will find normal, even if they're not queergender themselfs. Some will find insulting. Some won't be able to understand at all, but are going to try anyway, with good or bad results. Some have their own theories about what those people realy feel and do. And them you just picture how the character will counterreact.<br /> <br /> Do that, and everything else will fall in place sooner or later. Odd places, for sure, but that's precisely the point. You don't even have to present &quot;proper&quot; gay culture in your game to present a gay culture. Just imagine people feeling isolated and looking for equals that can form a supportive social group, and let this group develop its own culture, that's pretty much it. You'll only have to remind your players its a fictional culture, not really a big deal in an RPG.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T22:28:41-07:00","id":1212941,"title":"","content":"Resurrecting topic, lately there was published <b>Beast Players's Guide </b>( de facto <b>BtP</b> corebook, part 2 <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) and inside there is new Family ( X-splat ) -<i> Inguma</i>, Nightmares of Other in society.<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1193199-bpg-inguma-%E2%80%93-family-of-outsiders-%E2%80%93-and-minorities\"> I ( and some other STs ) plan to shamelessly used those as representation of various minorities</a>, LGBT+ people included. Right now I work to steal famous 2E Werewolf power to change sex - <i>Luna's Embrace</i> - and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1193199-bpg-inguma-\u2013-family-of-outsiders-\u2013-and-minorities?p=1212781#post1212781\">encode it somehow for Inguma to use</a>. Details at last link. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Notice: </b>After almost 3 years pause, I think topic should be rename into... <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">LGBT+ in CoD games </span></b><br /> <br /> as terminology in community changed a bit and whole nWoD brand become CoD of course. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T23:03:04-07:00","id":1212951,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ll be the dissenting voice here and say that the Begotten aren\u2019t exactly a good metaphor for representing the oppressed minority, Inguma or not, and LGBT+ or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T23:45:46-07:00","id":1212963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/570091-lgbtq-in-cofd-games?p=1212951#post1212951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019ll be the dissenting voice here and say that the Begotten aren\u2019t exactly a good metaphor for representing the oppressed minority, Inguma or not, and LGBT+ or not.</div> </div> </div> </div><b><i>A Fearful Lesson </i></b>chapter from <b>Dark Eras Companion </b>does not agree with you - if Beasts are good allegory on racial tensions in 19th century USA, they can work as allegory for LGBT+ people in modern world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Eras Companion, page 242</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Supernatural Stalemate</b><br /> What does this mean for Beasts?<br /> Beasts come from all walks of life, their inner natures poorly understood by even the most learned occultists. The Begotten may not be wholly human, but nevertheless carry their childhood prejudices and assumptions forward with them.<br /> <br /> A freedman Nemesis may fight to punish former slave masters; while a Confederate veteran Tyrant chooses instead to feed on the nightmares of Yankees he holds responsible for ruining his society. And the Ravager, whose childhood home burned in the war, is angry at everyone.<br /> <br /> To a certain extent, this makes life easy for Beasts. Begotten, after all, hold themselves accountable to nothing except their Horrors. The racial and class anxieties in the South offer a delicious spread of fears to feed their Horrors. Even if an individual Beast does not necessarily possess any egregious bigotry, he\u2019s usually not above exploiting such fears to get a good meal.<br /> <br /> Observing how Beasts interacted with the South may offer a clearer perspective on why Reconstruction failed. After all, a Beast\u2019s most emotionally (and ethically) fulfilling meal usually comes when her victim learns an important lesson. Without a sense of purpose or cultural unity, these lessons lose their meaning. A white supremacist might wake up to the pain she has caused, but a different man gets taught the perils of supporting black voting rights.<br /> <br /> Eventually, any meaningful signal gets lost and everything becomes little more than noise. Prejudice reinforces prejudice, and no one can find their way forward.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Eras Companion, page 243</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Community Ties</b><br /> For Beasts, the closeness of Southern communities becomes a double-edged sword. Young Beasts who have yet to realize their full potential feel their isolation even more keenly, as they struggle to make the social connections which come so easily to others.<br /> <br /> Though the Devouring brings self-actualization, a Southern Beast faces even more isolation. She lives in close, intimate quarters with those whom she loves but cannot entirely stop thinking of as prey. She may resist by declaring herself the protector of her community, refusing to feed on her neighbors and instead sating her hunger on those who have caused harm.<br /> <br /> When Sue Ellen is raped, the hoodoo witch she goes to might very well be a Nemesis, who sustains herself for years by repeatedly punishing (an outsider might say torturing) her rapist. Other Beasts, though, thrive on the fear generated by racialized hate. Even for Beasts with little or no racial prejudice, few see anything wrong with putting on a white hood, if doing so satisfies their Horror. Yet, though Beasts often accept without question others of their own kind, some find exploiting racial hatred a bridge too far.<br /> <br /> Such a commitment to community protection invariably comes with a price. The majority of Southerners live in small, sparsely-populated towns. This, to a Beast, means greater difficulty finding those who meet not only her Horror\u2019s particular needs for feeding, but her personal standards as well. Eventually, the Beast misjudges her Hunger or goes too long without hunting, and her Horror compels her to feed on a loved one. Now the Beast feels ashamed, angry at herself for failing in her chosen role.<br /> <br /> Even worse, her mistake may attract the attention of a Hero. Rounding up an angry mob to go take care of a threat isn\u2019t difficult in the South, especially if the Hero can take advantage of racial animosity. Even if the Beast escapes, she must bear the burden of knowing she brought the wrath of the Hero down on her loved ones.<br /> <br /> Some Beasts, then, make the painful choice to leave, to deliberately stay away from their people in order to protect them. Where can a Beast go and stay truly isolated, though? Even if a Beast moves away from her childhood home and settles in a different town or city, she still must face the risk she presents to her new community.<br /> <br /> Sometimes a Beast gives up having a stable home in the mortal world altogether, and takes to the road. The traveling salesman or peddler might not succeed exceptionally well in the economically depressed South, but at least he has an excuse to be constantly traveling and meeting new people. As the South slowly industrializes, railroad or telegraph employees can also stay transient.<br /> <br /> Other Beasts speak of small neighborhoods, rural towns, or desperately poor farm villages, where a Beast actually confessed what they were and still found acceptance. The name of the town changes with every telling, though. When a Beast arrives at this legendary place, they often find the story to be just a tall tale. They don\u2019t stop hoping, though, and continually seek a place they might find true acceptance.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T00:37:45-07:00","id":1212975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/570091-lgbtq-in-cofd-games?p=1212963#post1212963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b><i>A Fearful Lesson </i></b>chapter from <b>Dark Eras Companion </b>does not agree with you - if Beasts are good allegory on racial tensions in 19th century USA, they can work as allegory for LGBT+ people in modern world.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Last time I read that chapter, it was less a one-to-one, on-the-nose allegory and more a \u201cpeople will be people, and all sides have its monsters.\u201d<br /> <br /> I guess it could work if you\u2019re willing to admit the existence of monsters in whatever minority group, race or gender, you try to make the Begotten a symbol of. Not just the victim-turned-avenger type of monstrosity, nor monsters for whom their status as a minority is a redeeming quality, but people who are simply monsters. Because that\u2019s what the Begotten are. (I find the Daksha from Mage a prime example of \u201cNo, not all people are liberal and tolerant just because they\u2019re non-binary.\u201d)<br /> <br /> Of course, this sort of stance hardly wins support from said minorities, so leave it be if you will.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I find Prometheans better as an allegory for minorities and outsiders (althought Prometheans are more relevant to adolescence and \u201craised by wolves\u201d children). And no, the New Dawn isn\u2019t abandoning who you are to fit in with the majority; that\u2019s being stuck in Aurum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 04-29-2018, 03:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T05:37:14-07:00","id":1213019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/570091-lgbtq-in-cofd-games?p=1212975#post1212975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess it could work if you\u2019re willing to admit the existence of monsters in whatever minority group, race or gender, you try to make the Begotten a symbol of. Not just the victim-turned-avenger type of monstrosity, nor monsters for whom their status as a minority is a redeeming quality, but people who are simply monsters. Because that\u2019s what the Begotten are. (I find the Daksha from Mage a prime example of \u201cNo, not all people are liberal and tolerant just because they\u2019re non-binary.\u201d)</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there is also whole <i>'Society THINKS that we are monsters'</i> take. I was raised in 90s-00s Poland - do not get me start it how many times I heard that ( future ) LGBT was 'immoral', 'psychotic' or just 'stealing our children'. What's more - even when I'm just after 30 year old - I STILL hear those stories in public debates in my country. Maybe in more civilized countries of West it's not a problem - but in here, we day to day see that for large part of the society - we still are monsters. And they are <b><i>terrified</i></b> of us. ( Probably hard electorate of now ruling PiS party, so probably 20% of society, circa about. )<br /> <br /> Which works with how Begotten are representing things people are afraid of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-29-2018, 08:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T05:53:53-07:00","id":1213024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/570091-lgbtq-in-cofd-games?p=1213019#post1213019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, there is also whole <i>'Society THINKS that we are monsters'</i> take. I was raised in 90s Poland - do not get me start it how many times I heard that ( future ) LGBT was 'immoral', 'psychotic' or just 'stealing our children'. What's more - even when I'm just after 30 year old - I STILL hear those stories in public debates in my country. Maybe in more civilized countries of West it's not a problem - but in here, we day to day see that for large part of the society - we still are monsters. And they are <b><i>terrified</i></b> of us. ( Probably hard electorate of now ruling PiS party, so probably 20% of society, circa about. )<br /> <br /> Which works with how Begotten are representing things people are afraid of.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, but the Begotten don't stop at merely representing Who Are Feared. They're the ones who say &quot;You call me a monster? Then I will BE a monster!&quot; And that's why I'm asking you whether you are <i>really </i>okay with the implications of Begottenhood. You become the monster They say you are, <i>justifying </i>their prejudices in a visceral way that no minority people in real life are fortunately unable to. If that's where you're willing to explore, then by all means fire away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T15:33:01-07:00","id":1213545,"title":"","content":"I haven't seen it in this thread yet, but in the <i>Summoners</i> book there's a goetia (oops, mixed up my ephemerals) called Uther's Bliss, a personification of requited love. Here's the excerpt about it:<br /> <i>&quot; Facing down rogue Banishers and rampaging spirits was never the hard part for Uther, Thyrsus and Banner Warden of the Adamantine Arrow. No, that was </i><i>the years-long struggle to work up enough courage to finally come out to Slingshot and confess that his feelings for the Enchanter went deeper than just friendship.</i><i> The moments leading up to that revelation were the longest and most difficult of the Shaman\u2019s life. When Slingshot replied with a passionate kiss, though, Uther knew that this uphill battle against his own fear was, at long last, over. &quot;</i><br /> <br /> If you want more characters who are Gender and Sexual Minorities, just add it to their character. Not every gay character had a tough coming out and is a flag-wearing, pride-parade organizer. Sometimes you're just a normal person who is gay, came out, and that was that. Sometimes you don't even have to mention it in the backstory. It's just a fact. Yeah, it's a potential avenue for backstory, but sometimes you just want a gay character and being gay is a minor facet of his personality. Another good way is to make LGBT+ characters just exist if you're the ST for the session. The Prince's Sheriff has a human lover that you're going to blackmail him with to get him to leave your group alone. The neighboring pack alpha is blessed by Luna and switches physical gender as they please. If you aren't the ST, ask them about including these kinds of changes to your setting. These are fantasy games, and making your setting more open to LGBT+ characters (playable and non) is just realization that characters can be anything you want, and personality traits that flesh your characters out should not be punished with discrimination.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":19270,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19270-princevertigo","user":"PrinceVertigo","date":". 05-06-2018, 10:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19270-princevertigo","name":"PrinceVertigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar19270_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T16:39:26-07:00","id":1213574,"title":"","content":"I thought Uther's Bliss was a Goetia","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T16:40:26-07:00","id":1213575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PrinceVertigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/570091-lgbtq-in-cofd-games?p=1213545#post1213545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't seen it in this thread yet, but in the <i>Summoners</i> book there's a spirit called Uther's Bliss, a personification of requited love. Here's the excerpt about it:<br /> <i>&amp;quot; Facing down rogue Banishers and rampaging spirits was never the hard part for Uther, Thyrsus and Banner Warden of the Adamantine Arrow. No, that was </i><i>the years-long struggle to work up enough courage to finally come out to Slingshot and confess that his feelings for the Enchanter went deeper than just friendship.</i><i> The moments leading up to that revelation were the longest and most difficult of the Shaman\u2019s life. When Slingshot replied with a passionate kiss, though, Uther knew that this uphill battle against his own fear was, at long last, over. &amp;quot;</i><br /> <br /> If you want more characters who are Gender and Sexual Minorities, just add it to their character. Not every gay character had a tough coming out and is a flag-wearing, pride-parade organizer. Sometimes you're just a normal person who is gay, came out, and that was that. Sometimes you don't even have to mention it in the backstory. It's just a fact. Yeah, it's a potential avenue for backstory, but sometimes you just want a gay character and being gay is a minor facet of his personality. Another good way is to make LGBT+ characters just exist if you're the ST for the session. The Prince's Sheriff has a human lover that you're going to blackmail him with to get him to leave your group alone. The neighboring pack alpha is blessed by Luna and switches physical gender as they please. If you aren't the ST, ask them about including these kinds of changes to your setting. These are fantasy games, and making your setting more open to LGBT+ characters (playable and non) is just realization that characters can be anything you want, and personality traits that flesh your characters out should not be punished with discrimination.</div> </div> </div> </div>This does seem to be the direction that the published CofD games is taking. Rather than \u201cthey\u2019re (insert minority group), so of course they\u2019re Special and/or have this supernatural quirk.\u201d Making characters that are actual people, not just a bunch of profiles stapled on Status As A Minority.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T04:39:27-07:00","id":1214994,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Warning the Following is an opinion and might Offend, But it is not intended</b></u>.<br /> <br /> Honestly i feel the Best way to use LGBTQ characters.. is to not.<br /> *Watches the Tumbleweed and the pitchforks gather*<br /> Hear me out... I don't say not to have them. I mean Don't Force it, if someone is Trans... they are Trans, If someone is Homosexual they are Homosexual. That isn't and Shouldn't be the only Trait they have and it shouldn't be the only thing that Defines them. CoD (and oWoD before it) has never felt like the characters that represent that group of Humanity (and otherwise) are forced, they are people who just happen to be Trans/Gay/Bi Etc. THAT to me is the better way of having it.<br /> <br /> Sorry.. I might have just ended up sparking things. Conversation and discussion is always good.. And my post is not intended to bring offense, just something that I had to say. I've seen alot of Media that mishandles the subject and ruins things because it forces subjects they don't need to make an issue out of.<br /> <br /> I'm... gonna Shut up now before I put my foot in it anymore... (If i have)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T05:11:23-07:00","id":1214999,"title":"","content":"If you play in mostly Straight, White communities ( like I in Poland ) playing or running LGBT+ characters maybe only way to educate a bit your other players in lives of Non-Heteronormative people...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T05:13:40-07:00","id":1215000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/570091-lgbtq-in-cofd-games?p=1214994#post1214994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u><b>Warning the Following is an opinion and might Offend, But it is not intended</b></u>.<br /> <br /> Honestly i feel the Best way to use LGBTQ characters.. is to not.<br /> *Watches the Tumbleweed and the pitchforks gather*<br /> Hear me out... I don't say not to have them. I mean Don't Force it, if someone is Trans... they are Trans, If someone is Homosexual they are Homosexual. That isn't and Shouldn't be the only Trait they have and it shouldn't be the only thing that Defines them. CoD (and oWoD before it) has never felt like the characters that represent that group of Humanity (and otherwise) are forced, they are people who just happen to be Trans/Gay/Bi Etc. THAT to me is the better way of having it.<br /> <br /> Sorry.. I might have just ended up sparking things. Conversation and discussion is always good.. And my post is not intended to bring offense, just something that I had to say. I've seen alot of Media that mishandles the subject and ruins things because it forces subjects they don't need to make an issue out of.<br /> <br /> I'm... gonna Shut up now before I put my foot in it anymore... (If i have)</div> </div> </div> </div>PrinceVertigo also said something in that vein up above.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T05:55:08-07:00","id":1215007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/570091-lgbtq-in-cofd-games?p=1214994#post1214994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hear me out... I don't say not to have them. I mean Don't Force it, if someone is Trans... they are Trans, If someone is Homosexual they are Homosexual. That isn't and Shouldn't be the only Trait they have and it shouldn't be the only thing that Defines them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those aren't really the same thing. 'Force' implies there's some kind of incongruity to the character, whilst what you're describing are flat characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T06:21:17-07:00","id":1215012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/570091-lgbtq-in-cofd-games?p=1215007#post1215007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Those aren't really the same thing. 'Force' implies there's some kind of incongruity to the character, whilst what you're describing are flat characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>By Force I mean in a Narrative sense. Don't try to put a Square Peg in a round Hole type of thing.<br /> <br /> Like say: Harry Potter; Dumbledor is Gay. It's never mentioned in the story and only comes up because JK Rowling mentioned it AFTER the Books came out. The stories never needed that element in them, so it wasn't &quot;Forced&quot; into the story.<br /> If it's Needed in the story that's being told then sure, Let it be known. But it's not something that needs to be on every character at the introduction. (PC's are different, but NPC's unless its Integral too the character it's not needed)<br /> <br /> How many offensive characters were written that are Gay and that's it? That is their SOLE element that makes them up they aren't a Character.. they are a Caracature. They are brought into the Story as &quot;The Gay Friend&quot; or &quot;The Bisexual weirdo&quot; that shouldn't be why a character exists. If the character is Gay then fine, but it's not something that needs to be Rammed down peoples throats. The best character's are people first. One part of them is their Sexuality... It shouldn't be the only thing that defines them.<br /> <br /> Sorry if i'm just repeating, but it's just something that irks me. I'm fine with Gay/Bi/Trans People and Characters... But the more they are Made into an &quot;Issue&quot; the less they get accepted. Treat them as people, treat them just the same as everyone else you know, they are a Person after all.<br /> <br /> And yes I get the point about Flat characters, but too me the more they are made into &quot;Look at them they are Gay!&quot; the less they are an actual Character. Too many ties i've seen characters introduced just to be the &quot;Gay one&quot; &quot;The Black one&quot; &quot;The Girl&quot; and it's wrong. Don't treat them like that.<br /> CoD doesn't seem to do that too often (I don't think i have any examples of them doing it at all, which is Good).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":3981,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","user":"RickmanUK","date":". 05-04-2018, 09:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T07:36:29-07:00","id":1215042,"title":"","content":"I remember something back from the Fetches preview for Changeling, back when it was by David Hill. It went something like \u201cShe went into the house. Her wife was...\u201d I remember a lot of people noticing how just plain and obvious it was, in the sense of \u201cYes, she has a wife. Why do you ask?\u201d It\u2019s beyond mere acceptance. It\u2019s made into the default.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m cismale and heterosexual, so pardon me if I\u2019m clearly missing something here, but the sheer naturalness of such presentations (including Dumbledore\u2019s example up there) in fiction fascinate me. And when I put down the book I realize the real world is not even near that, so it makes me notice those things. That the real world is unfair, that real people are suffering out there. Just my two cents. <br /> <br /> (And now the inner Free Councillor in me is urging me to continue the war against the Exarchs, specifically the Father, so I\u2019ll be off now)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T10:50:54-07:00","id":1215145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/570091-lgbtq-in-cofd-games?p=1215012#post1215012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By Force I mean in a Narrative sense. Don't try to put a Square Peg in a round Hole type of thing.<br /> <br /> Like say: Harry Potter; Dumbledor is Gay. It's never mentioned in the story and only comes up because JK Rowling mentioned it AFTER the Books came out. The stories never needed that element in them, so it wasn't &quot;Forced&quot; into the story.<br /> If it's Needed in the story that's being told then sure, Let it be known. But it's not something that needs to be on every character at the introduction. (PC's are different, but NPC's unless its Integral too the character it's not needed)</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with Dumbledore is, invisible representation isn\u2019t representation at all. Sure, it wasn\u2019t important to the story that Dumbledore was gay, and that\u2019s fine. There\u2019s nothing wrong with that. But JK doesn\u2019t then get to take credit for writing one of the most important characters in her series as a gay man. Because she didn\u2019t write him as a gay man. Dumbledore\u2019s sexuality is entirely up to audience interpretation, whatever JK may claim, because it never actually comes up in the books. Which again, is fine, it just isn\u2019t gay representation.<br /> <br /> I also feel like \u201cit never came up because it was never relevant to the story\u201d is a poor excuse, because the author is in full control of what is and isn\u2019t relevant to the story. There\u2019s no reason JK couldn\u2019t have made Dumbledore\u2019s gayness matter if it had been important to her.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/570091-lgbtq-in-cofd-games?p=1215012#post1215012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How many offensive characters were written that are Gay and that's it? That is their SOLE element that makes them up they aren't a Character.. they are a Caracature. They are brought into the Story as &quot;The Gay Friend&quot; or &quot;The Bisexual weirdo&quot; that shouldn't be why a character exists. If the character is Gay then fine, but it's not something that needs to be Rammed down peoples throats. The best character's are people first. One part of them is their Sexuality... It shouldn't be the only thing that defines them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely. Tokenism and one dimensional stereotyping are definite pitfalls to watch out for. But I feel like people make it out to be much harder to visibly represent LGBTQIA characters without falling into those pitfalls than it actually is. As if invisibility and obnoxious stereotypes are the only options.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/570091-lgbtq-in-cofd-games?p=1215012#post1215012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry if i'm just repeating, but it's just something that irks me. I'm fine with Gay/Bi/Trans People and Characters... But the more they are Made into an &quot;Issue&quot; the less they get accepted. Treat them as people, treat them just the same as everyone else you know, they are a Person after all.<br /> <br /> And yes I get the point about Flat characters, but too me the more they are made into &quot;Look at them they are Gay!&quot; the less they are an actual Character. Too many ties i've seen characters introduced just to be the &quot;Gay one&quot; &quot;The Black one&quot; &quot;The Girl&quot; and it's wrong. Don't treat them like that.<br /> CoD doesn't seem to do that too often (I don't think i have any examples of them doing it at all, which is Good).</div> </div> </div> </div>Treat these characters as people, yes, but also don\u2019t rob them of their queer identity in so doing. For a good example, look at Ruby and Sapphire in Steven Universe. They are both female-coded, and they are in love. It isn\u2019t \u201cmade an issue of\u201d, but nor is it hidden. They are clearly, visibly lesbian, and neither of them is a hollow stereotype. They\u2019re just two people who love each other and are both women. Treating queer characters as people is absolutely the key, but treating them as people doesn\u2019t have to mean hiding the fact that they\u2019re queer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 05-04-2018, 01:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T11:08:34-07:00","id":1215154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/570091-lgbtq-in-cofd-games?p=1215042#post1215042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember something back from the Fetches preview for Changeling, back when it was by David Hill. It went something like \u201cShe went into the house. Her wife was...\u201d I remember a lot of people noticing how just plain and obvious it was, in the sense of \u201cYes, she has a wife. Why do you ask?\u201d It\u2019s beyond mere acceptance. It\u2019s made into the default.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m cismale and heterosexual, so pardon me if I\u2019m clearly missing something here, but the sheer naturalness of such presentations (including Dumbledore\u2019s example up there) in fiction fascinate me. And when I put down the book I realize the real world is not even near that, so it makes me notice those things. That the real world is unfair, that real people are suffering out there. Just my two cents.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s exactly the goal. We want to normalize queerness in fiction so the people who grow up with that fiction hopefully grow up viewing it as normal. Sort of a \u201cbe the change you want to see in the world\u201d type thing. That\u2019s also why Dumbledore doesn\u2019t work. Because the books don\u2019t treat him being gay as normal. They don\u2019t treat him being gay as anything, because they bever actually acknowledge it. And it would have been incredibly easy to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T11:30:17-07:00","id":1215171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/570091-lgbtq-in-cofd-games?p=1215154#post1215154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That\u2019s exactly the goal. We want to normalize queerness in fiction so the people who grow up with that fiction hopefully grow up viewing it as normal. Sort of a \u201cbe the change you want to see in the world\u201d type thing. That\u2019s also why Dumbledore doesn\u2019t work. Because the books don\u2019t treat him being gay as normal. They don\u2019t treat him being gay as anything, because they bever actually acknowledge it. And it would have been incredibly easy to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a Noble goal and one I Fully Support, I think I come across as bitter because to me seeing it handled well is Rare.. and it makes me annoyed at seeing it bad. Sorry if i Come across as a &quot;Hater&quot; I don't have any issues with it at all. I'm much more invested in the Story of what's happening and the Romance etc if it feels natural (Granted i see jokes in some things about Romance that makes me chuckle).<br /> <br /> Also i do get it with Dumbledore (My spelling is bad at times.. especially if I'm only half awake) He's not Representation, Probably a really bad example. One I'd say I find Ok (Or atleast better) is the Police Chief from the Flash series. Then again I could be wrong, and he might not be that good Representation either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T11:38:45-07:00","id":1215176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/570091-lgbtq-in-cofd-games?p=1215171#post1215171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a Noble goal and one I Fully Support, I think I come across as bitter because to me seeing it handled well is Rare.. and it makes me annoyed at seeing it bad. Sorry if i Come across as a &amp;quot;Hater&amp;quot; I don't have any issues with it at all. I'm much more invested in the Story of what's happening and the Romance etc if it feels natural (Granted i see jokes in some things about Romance that makes me chuckle).</div> </div> </div> </div>No worries, I got where you\u2019re coming from. Just wanted to add to your comment moreso than correct it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/570091-lgbtq-in-cofd-games?p=1215171#post1215171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also i do get it with Dumbledore (My spelling is bad at times.. especially if I'm only half awake) He's not Representation, Probably a really bad example. One I'd say I find Ok (Or atleast better) is the Police Chief from the Flash series. Then again I could be wrong, and he might not be that good Representation either.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m not familiar with that series, so I couldn\u2019t say. But I\u2019d assume as long as he\u2019s explicitly gay and has some dimensionality, it\u2019s probably a decent example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T12:29:02-07:00","id":1215198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/570091-lgbtq-in-cofd-games?p=1215176#post1215176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m not familiar with that series, so I couldn\u2019t say. But I\u2019d assume as long as he\u2019s explicitly gay and has some dimensionality, it\u2019s probably a decent example.</div> </div> </div> </div>He's the Chief first, determined to make sure everyone does their job, and wants to catch the criminals. The first you know about him being Gay is that he mentions it in a conversation. Well Mentions his Boyfriend brought him Lunch.. and that's it to introduce that fact. It's understated and not majorly &quot;Important&quot; at that point, but slowly becomes abit more for the character as the show goes on. It felt right, not forced or rushed. Atleast to me personally.<br /> <br /> Anywho, thanks for understanding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T14:22:34-07:00","id":1215230,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> Ah, it\u2019s indeed difficult, achieving that sweet spot of writing Still thanks for the input - it helps a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-11T10:41:11-07:00","id":1217713,"title":"","content":"I know it's a Beast but idea can be cool - male Inguma Tempter who seduces priests to sex with him, and breaking their vows of chastity, with bonus points for engaging in same sex physical actions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-11-2018, 03:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-11T18:39:27-07:00","id":1217851,"title":"","content":"Demons run all across the spectrum and then some - a Demon can be heterosexual, homosexual, bisexual, omnisexual or even asexual, simply by nature of their Cover and how they interact with said Cover. A Demon may not be attracted to humans but keep up the sexuality of their Covers simply for Covers sake. A Demon may simply be themselves in their first Cover, as if it is just <i>them</i>, including an attraction to said gender or lack thereof no matter what their Cover is supposed to be into. Heck, a Demon couple may be in love with one another no matter what Cover each other is inhabiting. It's the beauty of a game where you're roleplaying someone who is actively roleplaying as someone else, and one reason I love playing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-11T19:18:19-07:00","id":1217861,"title":"","content":"Demon isn't a favored game of mine, but I have been using the term 'androsexual' for a demon who is attracted to males, regardless of their current cover's gender identity, as of late.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Currently Playing:</b> <i>A large, mixed splat game of <b>CofD</b>.</i> <b>As:</b> Seraph du Salomon, Voice on the concordance. Unsubtle man reluctantly participating in the business of Magi. Awakening 2E homebrew <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1338514-house-du-salomon-a-proximus-dynasty?_=1569864567692\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...=1569864567692</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","name":"Gryphon's Feather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2598_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"215"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-12T03:48:00-07:00","id":1217924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/570091-lgbtq-in-cofd-games?p=1217713#post1217713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know it's a Beast but idea can be cool - male Inguma Tempter who seduces priests to sex with him, and breaking their vows of chastity, with bonus points for engaging in same sex physical actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think many of us had this idea when seeing the Hunger for Temptation. Although mine is more &quot;make closeted gay men admit they are gay.&quot; Not necesserarily in public but that they identify as gay or bi afterwards.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-12T03:52:08-07:00","id":1217926,"title":"","content":"Yes, Tempters are ultimate enemies of hypocritical priests, 'family mans' and politicians! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-12T05:38:09-07:00","id":1217935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/570091-lgbtq-in-cofd-games?p=1212975#post1212975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And no, the New Dawn isn\u2019t abandoning who you are to fit in with the majority; that\u2019s being stuck in Aurum.</div> </div> </div> </div>In Promethean, the world isn't telling your character they should be human, it's telling them that they shouldn't be at all. The Pilgrimmage is on one level an extended insistence that yes they should - along with, ultimately, saying &quot;This is who I am, because I am real.&quot; and having the world blink first - sure they can fail, but success and failure is not dependent on any kind of accountability to the majority around them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-04T12:46:30-07:00","id":1242773,"title":"","content":"There's an example in the new Changeling: the Lost sourcebook that I really like, in the first of the in-universe fiction bits. The viewpoint character, Aimee, has just learned that her pre-Arcadia girlfriend was also taken by the Fae, and this conversation ensues:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u201cWait. I found you under your real name. Did they\u2026 did they not replace you too?\u201d<br /> Katrina shivered. Now that I was looking, the scales rippled too. Like mica and cobras and the inside of shells. \u201cShe was made of glass and she wanted to fight about it.\u201d<br /> \u201cWhat happened?\u201d<br /> \u201cI cracked her open and feathers poured out.\u201d<br /> \u201cI haven\u2019t. I mean, I didn\u2019t. I don\u2019t want to. Jesus, he has <i>kids</i>. He\u2019s a <i>he</i>.\u201d<br /> \u201cYeah, I know. I went looking for you after I got back, too. I can see why you might want to leave well enough alone. Not like you wanted to be him before.\u201d<br /> \u201cWell, Mom seems happy with him, and\u2026if Lucy can\u2019t tell, maybe it would be kinder to let her keep him? It seems cruel to just pop into her life and be like \u2018Hey, your husband is imaginary and I have to destroy him so I can have a name I don\u2019t want back. So how do you feel about a divorce and full custody of all these kids?\u2019\u201d </div> </div> </div>I think this strikes a perfect balance between two conflicting pitfalls of writing LGBTQ+ characters: namely, having them be solely defined by their queer status and having their queer status have zero impact on their lives. The first pitfall is obvious, the second one less so - &quot;write queer characters the same way you'd write straight characters&quot; is common and often-good advice, but it feels a little too glib. Yes, a lot of queer characters' stories will have nothing to do with their queerness, but at the same time, there are plenty of circumstances where my queerness <i>does</i> impact the way I interact with the world, and it's nice to have that represented on occasion. Here, Aimee's transness matters without being her only trait: it informs the way she approaches her fetch, but she's got a lot of other stuff going on too<br /> <br /> I also particularly appreciate the fact that she's trans <i>and</i> into women: there's a few misconceptions I've come across that assume this to be an impossible combination, from &quot;trans is just an extreme version of gay&quot; to &quot;well, if they preferred women, why didn't they just stay a man?&quot;. So it's nice to see some representation that counters these, and manages to feel entirely natural while doing so. My thanks go out to whoever wrote this bit of fic!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24314-itokro","name":"itokro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24314_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T22:50:42-08:00","id":1268178,"title":"","content":"Daksha Legacy in <b>Mage</b> are sorcerers that want to evolve in to 'next human beings stage' - that is also universally intersexs. Still, they are also racists, believing anyone else to be 'inferior' to them and their Coming Race - so they are dividing on good and bad representation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-27T09:46:30-08:00","id":1271167,"title":"","content":"We have another example casually mentioned in <b>CtL</b> 2E Companion <b>Oak, Ash and Thorn</b> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/entitlements-ctl2-oak-ash-and-thorn/\" target=\"_blank\">Entitlement section preview</a>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <i>'The Black King holds the gleaming sword, red blood dripping from the blade. Now he controls the Huntsman, at the small price of eternally betraying the only man he loves.'</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T14:37:31-08:00","id":1271587,"title":"","content":"So I've just read once again the Voice of an Angel, and it occurred to me that through this thread, no one has mentioned that Marco Singe, the loved and half mad Pain Prophet, was presented as someone who at the very least has some homosexual preferences. I mean, the first fiction in the first book for the first edition of the CofD has started with Singe talking about his father beating him due to him having some encounter with another boy when he 12. It feels like it should be noted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-18T09:58:43-07:00","id":1297750,"title":"","content":"As both a trans and gay woman this is interesting to read. I have to admit that my ideas for those games are usually very trans and very gay almost by default.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>itokro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/570091-lgbtq-in-cofd-games?p=1242773#post1242773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this strikes a perfect balance between two conflicting pitfalls of writing LGBTQ+ characters: namely, having them be solely defined by their queer status and having their queer status have zero impact on their lives. The first pitfall is obvious, the second one less so - &quot;write queer characters the same way you'd write straight characters&quot; is common and often-good advice, but it feels a little too glib. Yes, a lot of queer characters' stories will have nothing to do with their queerness, but at the same time, there are plenty of circumstances where my queerness <i>does</i> impact the way I interact with the world, and it's nice to have that represented on occasion. Here, Aimee's transness matters without being her only trait: it informs the way she approaches her fetch, but she's got a lot of other stuff going on too<br /> <br /> I also particularly appreciate the fact that she's trans <i>and</i> into women: there's a few misconceptions I've come across that assume this to be an impossible combination, from &quot;trans is just an extreme version of gay&quot; to &quot;well, if they preferred women, why didn't they just stay a man?&quot;. So it's nice to see some representation that counters these, and manages to feel entirely natural while doing so. My thanks go out to whoever wrote this bit of fic!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes to those two things! Which sourcebook is this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25136-kev\u00e4\u00e4n-neito","user":"Kev\u00e4\u00e4n Neito","date":". 03-18-2019, 01:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25136-kev\u00e4\u00e4n-neito","name":"Kev\u00e4\u00e4n Neito","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25136_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-18T14